STATEMENT: >>>
Grammar to load: `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-yaml` (nixpkgs, 0.7.2, `python313Packages`/`python314Packages` binding present).

Candidate items (node type, confirmed against upstream `tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-yaml`'s `src/node-types.json`): `block_mapping`, `block_mapping_pair` (a GitHub Actions workflow's `jobs:` keys are `block_mapping_pair` nodes under the top-level `jobs` mapping), `flow_pair` (the `{ key: value }` inline form).

Present in this repo today: 7 tracked files — `.github/actions/{assert-nix-config,git-bot-identity,warm-ifd}/action.yml`, `.github/workflows/{ci,devenv-test,update}.yml`, `devenv.yaml`.

Gap: this is under the ~10-file presence bar this survey used elsewhere, and the operator did not name YAML directly; it is filed here because the survey brief pre-scoped it (both as one of the languages to check a grammar for and as one of the UIDs to file). Whether it earns real extractor work is an open question for whoever grooms this backlog.
